                <pb facs="0669" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1602: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-15T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>84. Chinese-Eastern Railway holds bill for transportation of Czechoslovak troops
                    leaving Siberia of more than three million gold dollars. Non-payment of this
                    amount seriously impairs railroad by weakening its economic position.</p>
                <p>Ascertain discreetly whether cost transportation Czechoslovak troops is direct
                    obligation of Czechoslovak Government or whether France immediately responsible
                    therefor.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
